<section id="markdown-handoff" hidden aria-labelledby="article-markdown-heading">
<h4 id="article-markdown-heading">Take your Markdown</h4>
<p id="article-markdown-readiness" class="small" role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"></p>
<label class="check"><input id="markdown-include-title" type="checkbox"><span>Include the article title as a Markdown heading when available</span></label>
<p class="small">Copy Markdown text or save a .md file. No excerpt, description, filename field, or front matter is required. The same title choice applies to Markdown with page details.</p>
<div class="actions"><button id="copy-article-markdown" type="button" class="button" disabled>Copy article Markdown</button><button id="download-article-markdown" type="button" class="secondary" disabled>Download .md file</button></div>
<details id="markdown-source-panel"><summary>Inspect or manually copy the approved Markdown</summary><label for="article-markdown-preview">Article Markdown, available after review</label><textarea id="article-markdown-preview" rows="10" readonly spellcheck="false" aria-describedby="article-markdown-help"></textarea></details>
<p id="article-markdown-help" class="small">The body keeps its current Markdown, including unsupported syntax and literal HTML. Your destination can interpret HTML and load linked images differently. Inspect it before publishing. Source notes, review questions, and revision history are excluded. <a href="/help/markdown-export/#article-markdown" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Markdown export help (new tab)</a></p>
</section>
